From 8142ac4046503543efab6cf065be73df63f2189d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:18:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] xocl: include <drm/drm_print.h> for the DRM_*() log
 macros (Linux 6.19)

xocl_bo.c, xocl_drv.c and xocl_ioctl.c use DRM_ERROR(), DRM_WARN(),
DRM_INFO() and DRM_DEBUG(), which come from <drm/drm_print.h>. That
header used to be pulled in by <drm/drm_mm.h>; mainline commit
ea722522d505 ("drm/mm: replace drm_print.h include with a forward
declaration", v6.19) removed it, so the macros are undeclared on 6.19+
(7.0.0-x here). The macros themselves still exist.

Guard: none on purpose. <drm/drm_print.h> exists on every kernel the
tree supports (since 4.9) and is include-guarded; up to 6.18 it is
already included through <drm/drm_mm.h>, so nothing changes there.

Equivalence: exact. The DRM_INFO/WARN/ERROR/DEBUG definitions in the
6.8.0-147 and 7.0.0-31 headers are byte-identical
("[drm] " / "[drm:%ps] *ERROR* " prefixes, DRM_DEBUG gated by
drm.debug), so every message keeps its format and log level.

Upstream: XRT commit dd3d69add instead defines missing DRM_*() macros
as pr_err()/pr_warn()/pr_info()/pr_debug(), which drops the DRM
prefixes and moves DRM_DEBUG from drm.debug to dynamic debug. Not
taken.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h b/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
index a142b9a..3ed9ecd 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
+++ b/driver/xocl/xocl_drv.h
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #endif
 #include <drm/drm_gem.h>
 #include <drm/drm_mm.h>
+#include <drm/drm_print.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/poll.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
